# StatePort Site — licensing boundary

This repository is the public StatePort website. Its contents are licensed
per component as follows. This boundary is independent of the StatePort
implementation repository; no licence choice made there applies here, and
none made here applies there.

## 1. Source code — MIT License

The site's own source code — HTML, CSS, JavaScript, Python build and
validation scripts, GitHub workflow definitions, and Mermaid diagram sources
— is licensed under the MIT License. The full text is in
`LICENSES/MIT.txt`.

## 2. Documentation and written content — CC BY 4.0

The written content — documentation pages, tutorials, release-ledger text,
the Stateware whitepaper sources and their rendered readers, and the
walkthrough narration scripts — is licensed under the Creative Commons
Attribution 4.0 International License. The full text is in
`LICENSES/CC-BY-4.0.txt`.

## 3. Brand assets — all rights reserved

The StatePort name, the shell mascot (`assets/stateport-mascot-shell.svg`),
and assets derived from it (including `assets/favicon.svg`) are brand assets
of the project author and are **not** licensed for reuse. The mascot is
copied byte-for-byte from the StatePort implementation repository with the
author's permission; its provenance and checksum are recorded in
`PROJECT_DNA.yaml`.

## 4. Media captures — CC BY 4.0, with third-party service notes

Screenshots, the prototype walkthrough video, and diagrams in this
repository are original works of the project author, created from
public-safe fixture data, and are licensed under CC BY 4.0 like the other
written content. Third-party services used at build time (recorded in
`NOTICE`) retain their own terms; no third-party media, font, or stock
asset is redistributed in this repository.

See `NOTICE` for the full asset inventory and attribution review.
